{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_018hiFzk3k2gXja6jsVJt5My","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-user personal productivity system that has grown a substantial R&D mission-control surface on top. Grounded in the project docs:\n\n**Core purpose**\n- A **personal productivity / task-management system** for J.C. Liechty, where **plain markdown files are the source of truth** (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, etc.) â€” no database, no binary formats, everything stays readable/editable from any CLI or editor.\n- Tasks move through a defined lifecycle â€” **Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved for Later â†’ Restored** â€” with domain buckets (academic, commercial, family, writing).\n\n**What it ships (the two main programs)**\n- **`anchor_gui.py`** â€” a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server (binds `http://localhost:8777`, run as the persistent NSSM Windows service `anchor`) that generates the full browser dashboard and writes changes back to the markdown files via `/api/*` endpoints.\n- **`anchor.py`** â€” a CLI mirror of the same logic that also regenerates the static `dashboard.html`.\n- **`anchor_healthcheck.py`** â€” a daily 5 AM self-test (Task Scheduler) that parses every file, boots a throwaway test server, exercises every endpoint and the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (fully stubbed), and writes `health_reports/YYYY-MM-DD.md`.\n\n**The R&D \"control surface\" (its largest area of active development)**\n- A per-project **mission-control / \"Project Cockpit\"** for running the **trio of skills** â€” researchPrime (Research) â†’ Crucible (Planning) â†’ Foreman (Build) â€” as durable, server-side terminal sessions, evolved across four design generations (v1â†’v4, all built and merged to master; v4 merged 2026-06-13).\n- It provides: **real ConPTY terminals** in the browser (xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket / SSE), **per-session git-worktree isolation**, a **session model** with **cached, grounding-validated AI summaries**, per-lane **doc roles**, a **cost/tokens/time rollup**, a **Grass Catchers** idea board, **deliverable launch-by-type**, and an **engine toggle** (Claude â†” Gemini, Gemini research-only).\n- v4's north star: each lane is a **tile with one honest status light** (green=working Â· amber=needs-you Â· red=crashed Â· grey=idle/done); clicking expands an **inline panel** (summary on top, resizable terminal below) where a new session **auto-loads the lane's skill once and greets once** â€” fixing the earlier repeating-prompt bug.\n\n**Architectural constraints (self-imposed)**\n- **Python stdlib only**, with exactly **one declared exception**: the optional `pywinpty` (`import winpty`, lazy, in `pty_manager.py` only) for the terminal subsystem â€” enforced by `distro.py`'s import scanner.\n- **Single folder** (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), local Git, no OneDrive/syncing.\n- Branded as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢.\"\n\nIn short: **a markdown-backed personal task dashboard that has become a local web-based command center for orchestrating multi-agent (Claude/Gemini) R&D work.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4420,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"840faad5-78af-4db4-a89b-f1a4c1630136","uuid":"07fe8b8c-32a8-464d-aed9-a76b9927ec18","request_id":"req_011Cc1hprHLdvuNNJ37FrNpH"}
